```

This solution uses a breadth-first search (BFS) approach to simulate the rotting process. It initializes a queue with all the rotten oranges and counts the number of fresh oranges. Then, it iteratively rots all adjacent fresh oranges, updating the grid and reducing the fresh count. The process continues until either all fresh oranges are rotted or no more oranges can be rotted. The time complexity is O(n * m), where n is the number of rows and m is the number of columns, as each cell is processed at most once. The space complexity is also O(n * m) due to the queue used for BFS.
